{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"g-core","type":"group","x":-40,"y":680,"width":2920,"height":780,"color":"5","label":"Interview trunk  ·  levels 0–84, plus DP 85–98"},
		{"id":"g-stop","type":"group","x":-40,"y":2100,"width":2920,"height":360,"color":"2","label":"Stop lines"},
		{"id":"g-cp","type":"group","x":-40,"y":1520,"width":1880,"height":520,"color":"3","label":"CP add-on  ·  only after the trunk is real"},
		{"id":"g-method","type":"group","x":-40,"y":-40,"width":2480,"height":340,"color":"4","label":"How to study one item"},
		{"id":"g-tracks","type":"group","x":-40,"y":340,"width":2480,"height":280,"color":"6","label":"Pick a track before you open the catalog"},
		{"id":"g-spec","type":"group","x":1880,"y":1520,"width":1000,"height":520,"color":"1","label":"Specialist ceiling  ·  model + workload, not more trees"},
		{"id":"m1","type":"text","text":"1. Invariant\n\nOne sentence: what must stay true after every op.\nIf you cannot say it, you do not have the structure yet.","x":0,"y":20,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m2","type":"text","text":"2. Ops + real cost\n\nWorst vs amortized vs average.\nName the input that hits the bad case.","x":400,"y":20,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m3","type":"text","text":"3. When it wins\n\nWhat previous structure it beats, and on which workload.\nIf it never wins, skip the implementation.","x":800,"y":20,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"t-int","type":"text","text":"**Interview**\n\n0 → 84, plus 85–98 done, not skimmed.\nAwareness only: trie, DSU, Dijkstra, heap, segment tree.\nStop before suffix automaton and link-cut.\n\nDone when you can pick the structure before you code.","x":20,"y":400,"width":760,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"t-db","type":"text","text":"**Databases / search / infra**\n\nB+ tree, LSM, skip list, bloom, hash variants.\nSuffix array / FM-index, succinct rank-select.\nNot the CP string automata unless you index text.\n\nDone when you can name the I/O or memory model.","x":1620,"y":400,"width":760,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"L0","type":"text","text":"**0 · Foundations**\n\nProblem, ADT, DS, algorithm.\nBig-O / Ω / Θ, cases, amortized.\nRecurrences, Master, invariants, bits.\nComparison vs integer-RAM.\n\nGate: you can state a cost without guessing.","x":20,"y":760,"width":340,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"L7","type":"text","text":"**VII · Graphs core**\n\nAdj list default.\nDFS, BFS, 0-1 BFS.\nCycle, CC, topo, bipartite.\nBridges, SCC.\nDSU (compress + rank).\n\nBFS = unweighted distance.\nDFS = structure.","x":20,"y":1100,"width":330,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"m4","type":"text","text":"4. One failure mode\n\nUnbalanced BST, hash pile-up, Dijkstra + negatives, greedy with no proof.\nWrite the counterexample.","x":1200,"y":20,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m5","type":"text","text":"5. Implement the representative\n\nOne structure per layer. Variants are recognition, not projects.\nFrom scratch, no library.","x":1600,"y":20,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"m6","type":"text","text":"6. One forcing problem\n\nA problem you cannot solve with the previous layer.\nIf the old tool still works, you did not need this one.","x":2000,"y":20,"width":370,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"t-cp","type":"text","text":"**Competitive programming**\n\nTrunk first. Then 101–122, 125–133, 141–147.\nAdd rollback DSU and HLD.\nSkip research dictionaries.\n\nDone when a new problem maps to a known state or decomposition.","x":820,"y":400,"width":760,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"L3","type":"text","text":"**III · Pointers, LIFO/FIFO**\n\nSingly / doubly / circular list.\nStack, queue, deque, ring buffer.\nMonotonic stack/queue.\nTortoise-hare.\n\nO(1) edit only if you hold the node.","x":1140,"y":740,"width":330,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L4","type":"text","text":"**IV · Hashing**\n\nDirect address, map, set.\nChaining vs open addressing.\nRolling hash, bloom.\nCuckoo / perfect = recognition.\n\nAverage O(1), worst O(n). Load factor.","x":1500,"y":740,"width":320,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L5","type":"text","text":"**V · Recursion + search**\n\nRecursion, D&C, backtracking.\nBranch and bound.\nMeet-in-the-middle, bitmask enum.\n\nTemplate: choose → explore → unchoose.\n2ⁿ ok only if you can say why.","x":1860,"y":760,"width":320,"height":260,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L16","type":"text","text":"**XVI · Modern ceiling**\n\nFib/binomial heap, vEB, fusion.\nKD / R / range tree.\nLSM (RocksDB) vs B+ (read-heavy).\nSuccinct rank-select, learned index.\nRope, link-cut already passed.\nDynamic connectivity.\n\nPick a model (RAM, I/O, succinct) and a workload. Not another tree.","x":2400,"y":1560,"width":460,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"L1","type":"text","text":"**I · Linear memory**\n\nStatic array, dynamic array, matrix, string, bitset.\n\nContiguous layout, O(1) index, cache, ×2 resize → amortized append.\nRow-major vs column-major.","x":400,"y":760,"width":320,"height":240,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L2","type":"text","text":"**II · Scan, search, sort**\n\nLinear / binary / parametric search.\nTwo pointers, window, prefix, diff.\nKadane, merge intervals.\nQuadratic sorts → merge/quick → counting/radix.\nQuickselect.\n\nBinary search = monotonic predicate.","x":760,"y":740,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L6","type":"text","text":"**VI · Trees + heaps**\n\nN-ary, binary, traversals, BST.\nAVL, RB, splay, B/B+.\nBinary heap, heapsort, PQ.\nTrie / radix.\n\nHeap is not a search tree.\nRB ≈ std::map. B+ = disk.","x":2220,"y":720,"width":320,"height":300,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L8","type":"text","text":"**VIII · Weights + trees**\n\nDijkstra (non-neg).\nBellman-Ford (neg + cycle).\nFloyd O(n³).\nKruskal = sort + DSU. Prim.\nBinary lifting LCA.\nEuler tour, diameter, reroot.\n\nSPFA: know, don't default.","x":390,"y":1100,"width":340,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L9","type":"text","text":"**IX · Greedy + DP**\n\nGreedy needs exchange or stay-ahead.\nActivity, Huffman, fractional knapsack.\nDP: state, transition, base, order.\n1D, knapsack, LIS, LCS, grid, interval, tree, bitmask, digit.\nD&C / Knuth / CHT, matrix exp.\n\nNo named state = no DP.","x":770,"y":1080,"width":360,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"L10","type":"text","text":"**X · Strings**\n\nKMP, Z, Manacher.\nAho-Corasick.\nSuffix array + LCP (practical).\nSuffix tree, SAM (CP).\nBWT + FM-index (real indexes).","x":20,"y":1600,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"L11","type":"text","text":"**XI · Range queries**\n\nSparse table, sqrt decomp.\nFenwick, segment + lazy.\nPersistent segtree.\nTreap, policy tree, wavelet.\n\nFenwick = point upd + prefix.\nSegtree = general range.","x":400,"y":1600,"width":340,"height":250,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"L12","type":"text","text":"**XII · Tree decompositions**\n\nHLD → path = segtree.\nCentroid decomp.\nEuler-tour tree.\nLink-cut.\n\nStart of dynamic graph DS.\nNot interview default.","x":780,"y":1600,"width":330,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"L13","type":"text","text":"**XIII · Flow + matching**\n\nEK, Dinic (default), push-relabel.\nMin-cut, bipartite matching.\nMin-cost flow, Hungarian.\n2-SAT = implication + SCC.\nEuler path. TSP DP.","x":1140,"y":1600,"width":330,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"L14","type":"text","text":"**XIV · Geo + numbers**\n\nOrientation, hull, sweep, calipers.\nSieve, extgcd, mod inverse, CRT.\nFast pow, factor, dlog.\nFFT/NTT, Gaussian.\n\nExact under mod/overflow.","x":1500,"y":1600,"width":320,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"L15","type":"text","text":"**XV · Randomized / online / hard**\n\nSkip list (Redis idea).\nReservoir, competitive ratio.\nHLL, Count-Min.\nNP, approximation, PRAM.\n\nTells you when to stop seeking exact poly-time.","x":1920,"y":1600,"width":440,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"s-small","type":"text","text":"**Smallest working path**\n\n1. Foundations until costs are not guesses.\n2. Array + hash + two pointers + binary search + stack.\n3. Recursion → tree DFS → heap → graph BFS/DFS.\n4. Dijkstra + DSU + 20 classic DP states.\n5. Only then Fenwick / segment / trie / strings.","x":20,"y":2180,"width":900,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-trade","type":"text","text":"**Named trade-off**\n\nCoverage vs depth.\n180 implementations is wasted motion.\nOne representative per layer, plus when the siblings win, is the skill.\n\nIf a layer is weak, the next layer is memorization.","x":960,"y":2180,"width":900,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"s-gate","type":"text","text":"**Gate before the next layer**\n\nYou can draw the invariant.\nYou can name worst and amortized.\nYou have one problem the previous layer cannot solve.\nYou can say the failure mode out loud.","x":1900,"y":2180,"width":900,"height":220,"color":"5"}
	],
